sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Adjuster (React UI)
    participant API as Django REST API
    participant Q as Redis / Celery Queue
    participant W as Celery Worker
    participant O as Pipeline Orchestrator
    participant CM as Coverage Matcher
    participant EA as Exclusion Analyst
    participant AD as Adjudication Drafter
    participant T as Tools (deterministic)
    participant L as LLM Provider
    participant DB as PostgreSQL + pgvector
    participant SSE as SSE Stream

    U->>API: POST /api/adjudicate/ {claim_id, claimed_amount}
    API->>DB: create Job (status=QUEUED)
    API->>Q: adjudicate_claim_task.delay(job_id, ...)
    API-->>U: 202 Accepted {job_id}

    U->>SSE: GET /api/jobs/{job_id}/stream/ (Last-Event-ID on reconnect)
    SSE->>DB: replay event history for job_id
    SSE-->>U: id + event: status (replayed / current)

    Q->>W: deliver task
    W->>DB: update Job status=RUNNING
    W->>O: run(claim_id, claimed_amount)

    O->>DB: start_or_resume_step(coverage_matcher)
    Note over O,DB: atomic claim - unique (job,name) constraint prevents duplicate concurrent execution
    O->>CM: run(AgentInput)
    CM->>T: get_policy_version(claim_id)
    T->>DB: resolve PolicyVersion by claim_date
    T-->>CM: policy_version_id (+ version_mismatch flag)
    CM->>T: search_policy(query, policy_version_id)
    T->>DB: dense + keyword retrieval, RRF fusion
    T-->>CM: citations (chunk, page, section, version)
    CM->>L: stream_completion(prompt + evidence)
    loop token stream
        L-->>CM: token
        CM-->>SSE: publish event: token {agent, token}
        SSE-->>U: id + event: token
        CM->>DB: is_cancelled(job_id)?
    end
    CM-->>SSE: publish event: agent_complete {tokens}
    CM->>DB: record AgentRun + complete_step(coverage_matcher)

    O->>DB: start_or_resume_step(exclusion_analyst)
    O->>EA: run(AgentInput + coverage context)
    EA->>T: search_policy(exclusions, policy_version_id)
    EA->>L: stream_completion(prompt + evidence)
    loop token stream
        L-->>EA: token
        EA-->>SSE: publish event: token
    end
    EA->>DB: record AgentRun + complete_step(exclusion_analyst)

    O->>DB: start_or_resume_step(adjudication_drafter)
    O->>AD: run(AgentInput + coverage + exclusion context)
    AD->>T: calculate_payout(claimed_amount, limit, deductible)
    Note over T: deterministic - never LLM-computed
    T-->>AD: payout (exact)
    AD->>T: detect_anomaly(claim_id)
    T-->>AD: anomaly flags
    AD->>L: stream_completion(narrative prompt - no dollar figures)
    loop token stream
        L-->>AD: token
        AD-->>SSE: publish event: token
    end
    AD->>DB: record AgentRun + complete_step(adjudication_drafter)

    O->>DB: update Job status=WAITING_APPROVAL
    O-->>SSE: publish event: status {WAITING_APPROVAL}
    SSE-->>U: id + event: status
    Note over SSE,U: stream closes - human review pause, not a terminal state

    U->>API: POST /api/jobs/{job_id}/approval/ {decision, outcome, rationale}
    API->>DB: get_job_status(job_id)
    alt status != WAITING_APPROVAL
        API-->>U: 400 InvalidJobStateTransitionError
    else decision == reject
        API->>DB: record Approval(status=reject)
        API->>DB: update Job status=FAILED
        API-->>U: {status: rejected}
    else decision == approve / edit-and-approve
        alt decision == edit
            Note over API: requires original_recommendation + outcome + rationale, or raises MissingEditValuesError before any write
        end
        API->>DB: record Approval + update Job status=RUNNING
        API->>T: finalize_adjudication(job_id, approved_by, outcome)
        T->>DB: create Decision (final_payout, outcome, rationale)
        T->>DB: update Claim status=decided
        API->>DB: update Job status=COMPLETED
        API->>DB: AuditLog: finalized
        API-->>U: {status: approved / edited_and_approved}
    end

    U->>API: GET /api/jobs/{job_id}/trace/
    API->>DB: query AgentRun + AuditLog + Approval + Decision (scoped by job_id)
    API-->>U: full Agent -> Tool -> Evidence -> Approval -> Decision trace